{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.CategoricalMassMarkov","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.CategoricalMassMarkov","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.Torsion.HeckeMassElement"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalMassMarkov.ofHecke_φ_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalMassMarkov.ofHecke_φ_succ","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/CategoricalMassMarkov.lean#L94-L102","doc":"The global sections form the Φ-orbit: `φ_{n+1} = Φ(φ_n)`. The `φ_n` are\ngenuinely closed under the mass endomorphism, not an independent family. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalMassMarkov.ofHecke_φ_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalMassMarkov.ofHecke_φ_zero","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/CategoricalMassMarkov.lean#L89-L92","doc":"The level-`0` global section is the mass element itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalMassMarkov.ofHecke_Φ_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalMassMarkov.ofHecke_Φ_apply","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/CategoricalMassMarkov.lean#L83-L87","doc":"The derived mass endomorphism is genuine left multiplication by the mass\nelement — not a free field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalMassMarkov.ofHecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalMassMarkov.ofHecke","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/CategoricalMassMarkov.lean#L63-L81","doc":"**De-axiomatisation (bean `2g2u`): cross-wire to the real Hecke mass\nelement.** From `Φ_mass(β) ∈ H_n(R,q)` (a `HeckeMassElement`), build the\ncategorical-mass carrier with:\n\n- `Φ := (Φ_mass · —)`, left multiplication by the mass element — a genuine\n  `AddMonoidHom` whose additivity is `mul_add`, so `Φ` is *derived*, not\n  a posited field;\n- `φ n := Φ^[n](Φ_mass)`, the Φ-orbit of the mass element (the level-`n`\n  brane sections closing the arc).\n\nRequires `[CommRing A]` (the ground ring of the Hecke mass element); the\ncarrier itself stays over generic `[Ring A]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalMassMarkov.Phi_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalMassMarkov.Phi_add","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/CategoricalMassMarkov.lean#L58-L59","doc":"The mass endomorphism is additive on the substrate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalMassMarkov.Phi_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalMassMarkov.Phi_zero","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/CategoricalMassMarkov.lean#L55-L56","doc":"The mass endomorphism preserves the zero state (it is additive). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalMassMarkov.φ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalMassMarkov.φ","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/CategoricalMassMarkov.lean#L49-L49","doc":"The global sections `φ_n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalMassMarkov.Φ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalMassMarkov.Φ","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/CategoricalMassMarkov.lean#L47-L47","doc":"The Markov-trace mass endomorphism `Φ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalMassMarkov.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalMassMarkov.mk","kind":"ctor","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/CategoricalMassMarkov.lean#L45-L45","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalMassMarkov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalMassMarkov","kind":"structure","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/CategoricalMassMarkov.lean#L40-L49","doc":"Data for the categorical-mass Markov-trace endomorphism.\n\nA `definition` carrier: the substrate algebra `A`, the Markov-trace mass\nendomorphism `Φ` (an additive map), and the family of global sections\n`φ : ℕ → A` (the `φ_n` closing the arc). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:categorical-mass-markov","label":"prop:categorical-mass-markov","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/categorical-mass-markov.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}